// suffices):
//   - outReal: Schaff Trend Cycle, from 0 to 100.
//
// Element k of each output is the value at bar BegIdx+k of the returned
// [OutRange], and BegIdx is at least [Core.STCLookback]: a range that ends
// before it returns NBElement 0.
//
// The lookback includes the unstable period the Core holds for FuncUnstIdSTC
// (see [Core.SetUnstablePeriod]).
//
// A real output may be one of the inputs, the same slice, to compute in place;
// outputs may not otherwise share memory with an input or with each other.
//
// The error is [OutOfRangeStartIndex] or [OutOfRangeEndIndex] for a range
// outside 0 to [IndexMax] or ending before it starts, and [BadParam] for a
// parameter out of range, an input too short, an output empty or too short or
// memory shared otherwise. A slice whose capacity a three-index expression cut,
// as slices.Clip does, can escape the sharing check.
